From e79128718046405cbe3c4bc69c2a32f133960700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?ibrahim=20y=C3=B6ndemli?= <ket0x4@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:53:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 162/167] i2c: qcom-cci: reset controller on runtime resume

After TITAN_TOP_GDSC power-collapses between probes or idle periods, re-programming registers with cci_init() alone leaves the controller stuck on the first transfer ('master X queue 0 timeout' / -ETIMEDOUT, e.g. imx471 failing probe until another transaction happens). Call cci_reset() (which invokes cci_init() after reset completes) on runtime resume so every transfer works after runtime suspend.
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
index bd70c6bae..2dc056394 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
@@ -488,7 +488,12 @@ static int __maybe_unused cci_resume_runtime(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	cci_init(cci);
+	ret = cci_reset(cci);
+	if (ret) {
+		cci_disable_clocks(cci);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
